==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|estanson|lang=fro}}, {{term|estanchon|lang=fro}}, (Modern French {{term|étançon|lang=fr}}), from {{term|estance||a stay, a prop|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|stans||standing|lang=la}}, present participle of {{term|stō|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|stănʹshən}}, {{IPA|/ˈstænʃən/|lang=en}} ''or''
* {{rfv-pronunciation|lang=en}} {{enPR|stänʹshən}}, {{IPA|/ˈstɑːnʃən/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[File:Stanchions and velvet rope - 37th G8 summit in Deauville 002.jpg|thumb|Stanchions supporting velvet rope]]

# A [[vertical]] [[pole]], [[post]], or [[support]].
#* '''2013''', [[w:J. M. Coetzee|J. M. Coetzee]], ''[[w:The Childhood of Jesus|The Childhood of Jesus]]''. Melbourne, Australia: The Text Publishing Company. chapter 27. p. 268.
#*:He staggers against a '''stanchion''', trips over a rope, and tumbles into the space between the quay and the steel plates of the freighter.
# A [[framework]] of such posts, used to [[secure]] or [[confine]] [[cattle]].

